BT 1 0 0 1 0 56.2 Tm /F1 9.3 Tf 13.1 TL (Speech recorded in real environments often contains background noise. More importantly, that noise does not) Tj T* (always stay the same. For example, an office recording may contain steady air-conditioning noise, while a street) Tj T* (recording may include cars that appear suddenly and then disappear. A speech-enhancement method with one) Tj T* (fixed setting can struggle with these changes. Strong suppression may remove more noise but damage the speech,) Tj T* (while weak suppression may leave too much noise behind.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 59.85827 447.5189 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 30 Tm 13.1 TL /F1 9.3 Tf 0 0 0 rg (This project asks: ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (Can short-term modulation cues and frame-level SNR estimates be used to adapt noise) Tj T* (tracking and time-frequency suppression so that speech quality and intelligibility improve over) Tj T* (fixed-parameter spectral subtraction and Wiener filtering under non-stationary noise?) Tj T* ET
Q
